From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:50:09 -0700
Subject: [M152] Guard TextInputManager against re-entrant destruction during
 notify

Original change's description:
> Guard TextInputManager against re-entrant destruction during notify
>
> TextInputManager::UpdateTextInputState() notifies observers in the
> middle of updating its state. When a newly focused view replaces the
> active view, it first notifies observers that the previously active
> view lost its text input state. RenderWidgetHostViewAura forwards this
> to InputMethod::OnTextInputTypeChanged(), where third-party IMEs can
> run a nested message loop. Tasks run there, such as window.close(), can
> destroy the WebContents, which owns the TextInputManager, or destroy the
> newly focused view. UpdateTextInputState() then continued with
> `active_view_ = view` on the freed TextInputManager, or went on to use
> the freed view.
>
> 77d3b67459722 made RenderWidgetHostViewAura robust to destruction during
> these IME callouts, but its caller here was not.
>
> Add a WeakPtrFactory to TextInputManager, and after each notification
> in UpdateTextInputState() return early if `this` has been destroyed or
> `view` is no longer registered. This also covers the final
> notification, after which `active_view_` was read without checking
> that `this` was still alive.
>
> Bug: 568937999
